---
description: Ambient conventions for the train-search test assignment
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

- TypeScript strict, no `any`. Explicit types on public function signatures.
- Data fetching only via `lib/api.ts` — never raw `fetch()` inside components.
- Search state (`from`, `to`, `date`, `maxPrice`, `sortBy`, `sortOrder`) lives in the URL
  query string, not only in local component state. Any change to search
  updates the URL.
- Every view that fetches data needs an explicit loading state AND an
  explicit error state — the external API is deliberately slow/unreliable
  for this assignment, never let it look like a broken page.
- Booking 409 (not enough seats) is an expected business outcome, not a
  system error — show inline recovery UI, don't redirect away destructively.
- Mobile-first: ~60% of traffic is mobile per the brief. Design for a narrow
  viewport first, then widen.
- Don't add a new dependency without a one-line reason in chat first.
